// endpoint_set_workspace_one_shot.proto — SetWorkspaceOneShot: mark a
// workspace a one-shot after its creation, or unmark it. AGENT API section.
//
// A ONE-SHOT LANDS ITSELF WHEN ITS WORK IS DONE. A workspace created as one is
// told so in its first message (the repository's completion directive); an
// ordinary workspace whose agent commits to finishing the rest of its work
// unattended marks itself one here, and the answer carries the same
// directive, so a workspace that became a one-shot is told exactly what one
// created as one was told. The mark is what every surface draws a one-shot
// from (the roster's one-shot mark, WorkspaceStatus.one_shot); the daemon
// performs nothing on the agent's behalf: the agent carries the directive
// out.
//
// THE USER TAKING THE WORKSPACE BACK CLEARS THE MARK, with no ask: a prompt
// the user submits from the editor or the webapp clears it before the prompt
// is delivered, and so does reopening a closed one-shot (OpenWorkspace). A
// prompt another workspace's agent sent, or one the daemon submits, leaves
// it. The clear is this verb's unmark, asked by the user.
//
// THE MARK NEVER MOVES THE WORKSPACE IN THE SIDEBAR (owner request,
// 2026-11-03). A one-shot files itself into its repository's subsections like
// any other workspace, so marking or unmarking it leaves it where it is
// arranged, and an unmark asks it to file nothing.
//
// ANY CREATED WORKSPACE MAY BE MARKED, a child included. The mark decides only
// whether the workspace finishes unattended, never who may land it: every
// workspace may land itself, marked or not.
//
// A REPOSITORY'S MAIN WORKSPACE IS NEVER A ONE-SHOT: the workspace on the
// repository's main checkout sits on the main branch, lands nothing itself and
// splits its work off into created workspaces, so there is nothing for it to
// finish unattended. Marking one is refused (`main_workspace`) before anything
// else is decided about the mark. No create can make one: every created
// workspace is a new linked worktree, never the main checkout.

